1
00:00:09,156 --> 00:00:11,549
If nothing is carried
from moment to moment,

2
00:00:11,629 --> 00:00:14,723
what makes a life one
life? A habit one habit?

3
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,148
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:22,106
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:22,916 --> 00:00:25,014
Part 1 let the passenger go.

6
00:00:25,094 --> 00:00:27,012
Change, without a changer.

7
00:00:27,092 --> 00:00:30,857
Part 2 turned the logic on the
questions we ask about anything,

8
00:00:30,937 --> 00:00:33,117
and found that they lose their object.

9
00:00:33,912 --> 00:00:36,825
One worry is left, and
it is the strongest.

10
00:00:36,905 --> 00:00:39,964
If there is no carrier,
what holds a life together?

11
00:00:40,044 --> 00:00:42,401
This part closes Section 4.

12
00:00:43,204 --> 00:00:45,710
The logic of substance has one answer.

13
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:48,414
Something persists. A soul.

14
00:00:48,494 --> 00:00:51,539
A stream of consciousness. A core self.

15
00:00:51,619 --> 00:00:53,441
The energy that is conserved.

16
00:00:53,521 --> 00:00:58,472
Each is proposed as what carries a
life, a habit, or a river through time.

17
00:00:59,288 --> 00:01:02,727
Take that carrier away,
the substantialist expects,

18
00:01:02,807 --> 00:01:05,992
and only a series of
disconnected flashes is left.

19
00:01:06,072 --> 00:01:09,552
Each moment sealed off
from the next. No memory.

20
00:01:09,632 --> 00:01:12,410
No responsibility. No learning.

21
00:01:13,212 --> 00:01:16,329
The logic of dependency
rejects both pictures.

22
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,834
The carrier, and the disconnection.

23
00:01:19,648 --> 00:01:21,719
The tradition's image is a lamp.

24
00:01:21,799 --> 00:01:26,162
The monk Nāgasena asks King Milinda
whether the flame of the last watch of the

25
00:01:26,242 --> 00:01:29,219
night is the same as the
flame of the first watch.

26
00:01:29,299 --> 00:01:33,132
Not the same, the king says.
And not another either.

27
00:01:33,212 --> 00:01:36,764
The light burned through the night,
in dependence on the same lamp.

28
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:40,195
Nothing passes from one flame to the next.

29
00:01:40,275 --> 00:01:43,469
And yet the second is not
unconnected with the first.

30
00:01:43,549 --> 00:01:47,273
Continuity is named on a succession
that is neither identical,

31
00:01:47,353 --> 00:01:48,895
nor wholly different.

32
00:01:49,704 --> 00:01:52,658
A melody known by heart
shows how this works.

33
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:56,218
Each playing is new, and none
of them is the previous one.

34
00:01:56,298 --> 00:02:00,294
No tune is stored somewhere between
playings, waiting to be released.

35
00:02:00,374 --> 00:02:02,957
Yet the tune is recognised
across them all.

36
00:02:03,037 --> 00:02:05,321
It can be played well or badly.

37
00:02:05,401 --> 00:02:07,142
Remembered or forgotten.

38
00:02:07,222 --> 00:02:09,035
Changed by practice.

39
00:02:09,844 --> 00:02:13,641
Habit, character, skill
and karma are like this.

40
00:02:13,721 --> 00:02:16,453
Each moment is conditioned
by what went before,

41
00:02:16,533 --> 00:02:18,994
and the link is valid and reliable.

42
00:02:19,074 --> 00:02:21,548
But the link is named across the moments.

43
00:02:21,628 --> 00:02:24,433
It is not carried by something
that runs through them.

44
00:02:25,232 --> 00:02:29,205
Two things follow. And I think they
are why this matters for a life,

45
00:02:29,285 --> 00:02:31,030
not only for an argument.

46
00:02:31,836 --> 00:02:37,453
Nothing is lost. Memory, responsibility,
learning and karma are all kept,

47
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:39,233
as designations that hold.

48
00:02:39,313 --> 00:02:42,997
The person who made a promise
forty years ago keeps it today.

49
00:02:43,077 --> 00:02:46,122
Not because a core self
crossed the years untouched.

50
00:02:46,202 --> 00:02:49,700
Because the conventional
I, found nowhere, works.

51
00:02:50,512 --> 00:02:55,097
And nothing is fixed. A continuity
not carried by an essence can bend.

52
00:02:55,177 --> 00:02:59,866
A habit can loosen. A character
can soften. A grievance can end.

53
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:03,253
There was never anything underneath
that had to stay the same.

54
00:03:04,052 --> 00:03:08,569
Continuity without a carrier is more
reliable than the nihilist expects.

55
00:03:08,649 --> 00:03:11,494
And more open than the
substantialist can allow.

56
00:03:12,288 --> 00:03:16,533
Someone trained in physics may feel
a carrier has been found after all.

57
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,136
Energy is conserved.

58
00:03:18,216 --> 00:03:21,873
It changes form, chemical
into heat, heat into motion,

59
00:03:21,953 --> 00:03:23,693
while the total stays the same.

60
00:03:23,773 --> 00:03:26,469
Surely energy is the modern substance.

61
00:03:27,268 --> 00:03:29,652
Physics itself does not treat it so.

62
00:03:29,732 --> 00:03:32,315
Energy is a quantity, not a fluid.

63
00:03:32,395 --> 00:03:35,752
A number, computed in different
ways for different forms,

64
00:03:35,832 --> 00:03:38,768
whose total comes out the
same before and after.

65
00:03:38,848 --> 00:03:40,779
Its amount depends on the frame.

66
00:03:40,859 --> 00:03:43,673
A moving ball has energy
relative to the ground,

67
00:03:43,753 --> 00:03:46,554
and none relative to a
runner keeping pace with it.

68
00:03:46,634 --> 00:03:49,149
And its conservation
comes from a symmetry:

69
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:52,070
the laws of physics do
not change over time.

70
00:03:52,150 --> 00:03:56,844
It is a feature of how regularities
hang together. Not a store of stuff.

71
00:03:57,656 --> 00:04:01,235
When a match burns, chemical
energy becomes heat and light.

72
00:04:01,315 --> 00:04:05,271
The sentence is correct, and the
regularity it records is among the most

73
00:04:05,351 --> 00:04:06,765
reliable there is.

74
00:04:06,845 --> 00:04:10,583
But nothing is found leaving the match
head and travelling into the flame.

75
00:04:10,663 --> 00:04:12,920
Conservation is a regularity.

76
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,732
It is not a passenger.

77
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:17,693
A subtler candidate remains.

78
00:04:17,773 --> 00:04:21,388
If nothing is fixed, appearances
seem endlessly plastic.

79
00:04:21,468 --> 00:04:24,554
The same lines seen as
a duck, or as a rabbit.

80
00:04:24,634 --> 00:04:28,997
Surely, then, there is a store of
possibilities behind appearances,

81
00:04:29,077 --> 00:04:30,741
from which each one is drawn.

82
00:04:31,552 --> 00:04:34,357
That gives emptiness a home behind things.

83
00:04:34,437 --> 00:04:39,484
It turns emptiness into a new substance,
made of possibilities instead of stuff.

84
00:04:40,292 --> 00:04:45,080
But a potential is identified only through
what it becomes, and what it meets.

85
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:48,138
Salt is soluble only in relation to water.

86
00:04:48,218 --> 00:04:51,371
A seed is a seed only in
relation to the sprout.

87
00:04:51,451 --> 00:04:54,591
Could, is said within a
framework of conditions.

88
00:04:54,671 --> 00:04:57,137
It is not a thing waiting backstage.

89
00:04:57,936 --> 00:05:00,075
Nor is the plasticity infinite.

90
00:05:00,155 --> 00:05:02,833
A rope can appear as a snake in dim light.

91
00:05:02,913 --> 00:05:05,795
A shadow cannot be walked
across as a bridge.

92
00:05:05,875 --> 00:05:08,282
Appearances are open because they depend,

93
00:05:08,362 --> 00:05:10,184
and limited for the same reason.

94
00:05:10,264 --> 00:05:13,648
This is the same luminous
plasticity of Section 3.

95
00:05:13,728 --> 00:05:17,969
Appearances arising exactly as
their conditions allow, and no more.

96
00:05:18,049 --> 00:05:19,790
Nothing blocks the display.

97
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:22,077
And there is no store behind it.

98
00:05:22,876 --> 00:05:25,980
The two logics also lay
out different paths.

99
00:05:26,792 --> 00:05:31,295
Under the logic of substance, the
path is a journey made by a traveller.

100
00:05:31,375 --> 00:05:33,455
Bad states are things to remove.

101
00:05:33,535 --> 00:05:35,616
Good states are things to acquire.

102
00:05:35,696 --> 00:05:39,352
Awakening is a place one
arrives at, and then keeps.

103
00:05:39,432 --> 00:05:42,396
Effort lifts out anger as
one would lift out a stone,

104
00:05:42,476 --> 00:05:45,004
and holds on to calm as
one would hold a coin.

105
00:05:45,084 --> 00:05:47,491
And because the states
are pictured as things,

106
00:05:47,571 --> 00:05:50,036
the effort tends to harden into grasping.

107
00:05:50,844 --> 00:05:55,076
Under the logic of dependency,
three things are recognised instead.

108
00:05:55,888 --> 00:05:57,524
Conditions are what work.

109
00:05:57,604 --> 00:06:00,147
Anger is not a thing with its own nature.

110
00:06:00,227 --> 00:06:05,473
It arises with a situation, a
body, a history, an interpretation.

111
00:06:05,553 --> 00:06:09,032
Change the conditions, and
the appearance reconfigures.

112
00:06:09,112 --> 00:06:13,466
Ethics, meditation and study are
ways of arranging conditions.

113
00:06:14,276 --> 00:06:17,135
Openness is not a virtue added on top.

114
00:06:17,215 --> 00:06:19,757
It is what being dependent already means.

115
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:23,344
If states had their own nature,
practice would be pointless,

116
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,903
because nothing could
become other than it is.

117
00:06:26,712 --> 00:06:31,487
And there is nothing to hold, and no one
apart from the holding. There is a path.

118
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:34,073
But no one walks it
apart from the walking.

119
00:06:34,876 --> 00:06:38,931
One trap remains, and I see
it as the habit's last refuge.

120
00:06:39,011 --> 00:06:43,727
Openness, non holding, and emptiness
can quietly become the new things held.

121
00:06:43,807 --> 00:06:48,292
A state to reach. An attitude
to keep. A view to defend.

122
00:06:48,372 --> 00:06:50,629
Openness, too, is empty.

123
00:06:50,709 --> 00:06:52,436
It is not something you have.

124
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:54,791
It is the absence of
what you were holding.

125
00:06:55,592 --> 00:06:57,731
Return to the candle of Part 1.

126
00:06:57,811 --> 00:07:00,951
It still burns down through
the night, the wax shortening,

127
00:07:01,031 --> 00:07:02,953
the flame leaning in the draught.

128
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:07,127
The logic of substance asks
what the flame really is,

129
00:07:07,207 --> 00:07:10,433
beneath its changing, and where
it will go when it goes out.

130
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:13,667
The logic of dependency
asks nothing of the kind.

131
00:07:13,747 --> 00:07:17,566
It notices that the flame was never
anything apart from the burning.

132
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:20,352
And the burning never
anything apart from the wax,

133
00:07:20,432 --> 00:07:22,842
the air, and the one who watches.

134
00:07:23,656 --> 00:07:26,230
Nothing is taken from the candle by this.

135
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:29,155
It gives exactly as much light as before.

136
00:07:29,972 --> 00:07:33,941
This is Section 4, Part 3 of
the Dependent Arising series,

137
00:07:34,021 --> 00:07:35,943
and the close of Section 4.

138
00:07:36,744 --> 00:07:39,766
What changes is only the weight
with which it is watched.

139
00:07:39,846 --> 00:07:43,167
And with that, the direction
of a life spent watching.

